  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Prompt Requirements**\n\nI\'m now carefully reviewing the prompt\'s requirements. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the product name and metadata. I must ensure the `metadata.json` file is correctly formatted, with the name set to \"NextBuild\" and a description of \"Student job-search tool turning resumes and GitHub profiles into actionable build roadmap.\" I have to be precise with this.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Aesthetics**\n\nI\'ve been thinking about the visual metaphors. I\'m aiming for a technical blueprint aesthetic, like an architect\'s drafting table. I\'m deliberately avoiding fake system-status text or jargon. The color palette is finalized: blueprint navy for background, drafting line blue for UI elements, chalk paper for primary text, signal amber for buttons, slate fog for secondary text, verified green for strong fit status, and muted red for \"needs work\" verdicts. I\'m using Space Grotesk for display and headings.\n\n\n**Specifying Font Families**\n\nI\'m now determining the font styles. Body text will be Inter (regular/medium). Data and technical values will use IBM Plex Mono. I intend to import these fonts from Google Fonts directly in the HTML or CSS. I\'m going with either a `<link>` or an `@import` tag in the `index.html` or `index.css`.\n\n**Crafting Hero Blueprint Diagram**\n\nI am now focusing on the signature hero element, which is a blueprint diagram. It is an SVG showing five connected stages using dashed connector lines. The stages are \"Resume + GitHub\", \"Job Description\", \"Fit Analysis\" with signal amber highlight, \"Roadmap\", and \"Applied.\" I want to have the connector lines animate to draw in from left to right on page load.\n\n\n**Refining Blueprint Animation**\n\nI\'m now delving into the animation details of the hero diagram. I\'m aiming for a visually engaging experience. I will use `motion/react` to animate each stage node to fade and scale in as the connector lines draw in. I\'m aware of the `prefers-reduced-motion` setting; if it\'s enabled, the animation will be skipped, and the fully drawn diagram will be displayed.\n\n**Defining Page Sections**\n\nI\'m solidifying the page structure, from top to bottom. The navbar features the \"NextBuild\" wordmark and \"Sign In\" and \"Get Started\" buttons. The hero section follows with a headline, body copy, the blueprint diagram, and a CTA button. Finally, I\'m designing the resume upload section, which includes a labeled drag-and-drop file zone. I plan to use custom styling for a dashed drafting-line border and chalk-paper styling.\n\n\n**Designing Resume Upload**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the resume upload section. I\'ve decided on a blueprint-styled card, centered with an upload icon and prompt text. I\'ll add a secondary button offering sample resumes. Post-selection, the interface will display the filename with a checkmark and remove link.\n\n**Defining GitHub Connectivity**\n\nI\'m moving onto the GitHub connection section. I\'ll label this \"Step 2\" and offer a styled input field for username or profile URL. A \"Connect\" button will be adjacent. Demo profiles will populate the UI. Post-connection, the interface will display a repo grid, featuring repo names, descriptions, and tech stack tags.\n\n\n**Structuring Job Section**\n\nI am now structuring the job description section. \"Step 3 \342\200\224 The Job You Want\" will feature a styled input field for a job posting URL, with sample job options. After fetching, I will present the job title, company name, and a short description. I\'m focusing on clarity and ease of use.\n\n\n**Constructing Actionable Roadmap**\n\nI\'m now outlining the actionable roadmap section. I will present 2-3 recommended project cards in a horizontal, drafted path layout on desktop and a vertical list on mobile. Each card will detail a project title, a problem statement, tech stack tags, and estimated build time. Clicking a card will expand to show a milestone-by-milestone roadmap.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 233946350
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
