    thinking: "**Defining Component Structure**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the modular component structure. I\'ve begun reviewing the necessary sections and components. So far, I have the `Navbar` outlined. It includes the logo with specific styling and a \"Sign In\" button with detailed design specifications.\n\n\n**Analyzing Hero Section Elements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `HeroSection`. I have defined the button with a Line Blue border. I\'ve fleshed out the \"Get Started\" button design specifications. I have written up the Headline and Body copy, with specified fonts and colors. Furthermore, I have defined the interactive SVG diagram. I\'ve begun to list the five stages with labels and the connecting animated lines between them.\n\n\n**Refining Step-Specific Components**\n\nI\'m making progress on the new sections, I\'ve outlined `ResumeSection` specifics including the drag-and-drop zone with its visual cues and secondary button. Then, I\'ve outlined the `GithubSection` details, focusing on the styled input field and \"Connect\" button design. I\'m focusing on the precise text, styling, and interactivity.\n\n\n**Defining Github Connection Details**\n\nI\'m now drafting the specifics for the Github connection component. I\'m focusing on the connected state badge, the grid layout and elements of the repository cards, and the styling for each of these elements, including the font and background. I am outlining specific requirements such as the use of Slate Fog / Drafting Blue background for the tech stack tag pills, and the styling of the repo cards. I\'m taking the sample Github user `alexdev-builds` into consideration while drafting.\n\n**Constructing Job Section Details**\n\nI\'ve been working on the `JobSection` now. The focus is now on the text input with a job posting URL and the \"Fetch Job\" button. I have incorporated the sample presets so the user can easily test the components. I am specifying the display of the job title, company name, and description excerpt after fetching, including their respective fonts.\n\n\n**Evaluating Fit Analysis**\n\nI\'m now focusing on evaluating the \"YOUR FIT ANALYSIS\" section. I have defined the verdict badge options and styling with colors and font specifications. I\'ve also outlined the project cards with project names, fit verdicts, and reasoning. Additionally, I\'ve specified a disclaimer at the bottom in Slate Fog. I will be incorporating the generated guidance.\n\n**Prioritizing Build Plan**\n\nI\'m now refining the \"YOUR BUILD PLAN\" roadmap section. I\'ve begun to define the horizontal and vertical layouts for desktop and mobile, respectively. Each card\'s elements, including project title, problem statement, tech stack tags, and estimated build time, are now fully specified in detail.\n\n\n"
