    thinking: "**Confirming Successful Build**\n\nI\'m pleased to report a flawless first build! The NextBuild project compiles without errors. I\'ve confirmed that the product name and context, specifically \"NextBuild\" as a student job-search tool, are accurately reflected. Both the `metadata.json` and `index.html` files now correctly feature the project title.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Design**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the visual design, aiming for a drafting table theme. I\'ve chosen a Blueprint Navy background with a subtle grid. Drafting Line Blue will be for borders, and Chalk Paper for text. I\'ve also incorporated Signal Amber for buttons and focus rings, Slate Fog for secondary text, Verified Green for confirmed matches, and Muted Red for \"Needs Work\" badges. No fake system status text; all text will be plain language. Space Grotesk for headings, Inter for body, and IBM Plex Mono for specific elements are being loaded via Google Fonts.\n\n\n**Mapping User Flow**\n\nI\'ve been mapping the user flow across eight key sections. The Navbar includes \"NextBuild\" and Sign In/Get Started CTAs. The Hero section provides a headline, body copy, diagram, and a CTA. Steps 1-3 involve resume upload, GitHub connection, and job description input, respectively. I\'m focusing on the visual flow and framer-motion animations, particularly the dashed connector lines, and respecting `useReducedMotion()`. I\'m using Signal Amber for active focus states on steps 2 and 3.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have built the single-page web app frontend for **NextBuild**:\n\n- **Visual Metaphor & Palette**: Designed around an architectural drafting blueprint theme utilizing exact color tokens (`#10253F` Blueprint Navy, `#3D6FB4` Drafting Line Blue, `#F2F0E6` Chalk Paper, `#F2A93B` Signal Amber, `#7C93AC` Slate Fog, `#4FA87B` Verified Green, `#C4634F` Muted Red) with clean, plain-language text and zero cryptic jargon.\n- **Typographic Hierarchy**: Paired Google Fonts with **Space Grotesk** for headings, **Inter** for body copy, and **IBM Plex Mono** for technical values, repo names, and stack tags.\n- **Signature Hero Blueprint Diagram**: Built an animated 5-stage SVG diagram (`Resume + GitHub` \342\206\222 `Job Description` \342\206\222 `Fit Analysis` \342\206\222 `Roadmap` \342\206\222 `Applied`) featuring dashed connector lines that draw on load and respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.\n- **Complete Page Flow**:\n  1. **Navbar**: NextBuild wordmark with \"Sign In\" and \"Get Started\" buttons.\n  2. **Hero Section**: Space Grotesk headline, explanatory lead copy, interactive blueprint diagram, and primary CTA.\n  3. **Resume Upload Section**: Custom drag-and-drop file zone, sample resume quick loader, and uploaded file confirmation state with remove option.\n  4. **GitHub Connect Section**: Profile connector input and 3-column repository card grid with tech stack pills.\n  5. **Job Description Section**: Job posting URL fetcher, preset job role buttons, and parsed requirement excerpts.\n  6. **Fit Analysis Section**: Large overall verdict badge (`Strong Match`, `Partial Match`, or `Needs Work`), project match evaluation cards, and the required AI guidance disclaimer.\n  7. **Roadmap Section**: Horizontal drafted path on desktop (vertical stacked list on mobile) featuring recommended project cards that expand to reveal sequential milestone implementation steps.\n  8. **Application Package Section**: Tailored resume summary, \"why this role\" blurb, copy buttons with feedback states, and tappable status tracker pills (`Saved`, `Applied`, `Interviewing`)."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 45394738
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
