  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Project Guidelines**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the prescribed setup for full-stack applications with Express and Vite. I\'m taking a close look at the provided scripts: \"dev\" runs `tsx server.ts`, and \"build\" executes Vite build along with an esbuild bundling of `server.ts` to a node-compatible CommonJS module, excluding external packages. This outlines the critical stages for development and production.\n\n\n**Verifying Package Dependencies**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that the necessary packages like `express`, `@google/genai`, and `esbuild` are already in place, according to `package.json`. Now, I am exploring whether we need additional helper packages, or if the current setup with Express and `@google/genai` is sufficient to implement all the required API endpoints. For the `server.ts` file, I am checking if `cors` or body-parsing middleware are needed. It seems Express 4\'s built-in `express.json` and `express.urlencoded` should suffice.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now concretely defining the API endpoints needed for the application. Specifically, I\'m working on the design for several API routes: fetching public GitHub repos, generating structured project summaries, parsing job descriptions, researching companies, analyzing candidate fit, generating project roadmaps, and creating tailored application packages. Each endpoint will have specific POST request structures for input parameters.\n\n\n"
